# TLS policy — the WORKSTATION copy. Mounted beside the Caddyfile as
# `mode.caddy`, replacing k8s/ingress/mode.caddy.
#
# A laptop cluster has no public IP and no inbound path, so an ACME challenge
# can never reach Caddy — issuance could not succeed here even if it were
# wanted. TLS terminates at Cloudflare's edge and cloudflared carries the
# request to this origin over a connection it dialled outbound.
#
# All three snippets are no-ops, and with SX_SCHEME=http every site block is
# served as plain HTTP on :80. There is no :80 → :443 redirect, because :80 is
# where the tenant catch-all listens (SX_CATCHALL=:80).
#
# Consequence to be aware of: the hop from Cloudflare to this machine is
# protected by the tunnel, not by a certificate Caddy holds. Set the zone's
# SSL/TLS mode to "Full (strict)" — do NOT use Flexible.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE ONLY DIFFERENCE between a workstation deployment and a cloud
# one. The routing table itself (k8s/ingress/Caddyfile) is byte-identical.

(tls_policy) {
}

(tls_managed) {
}

(tls_admin_origin) {
}
